30,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Oh dear, it seems some of our neighbors are quite isolated now. I worry that relying on the county buses might lead to more disappointments.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It is a quiet tragedy. I found that our outer wards are effectively cut off, and our physical hours are too restrictive for those using the catalogue at night.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,Guess what! We tried outreach before and people loved it! But we also tried a photo thing that was a total mess because they forgot to label them!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,Fascinating. It appears we have a habit of returning unused capital to reserves while our operational lines are bleeding. A most elegant way to go broke.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"My findings are concerning. We have the passion of volunteers, but we lack the internal supervisory skills and the technical certifications to maintain safety.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, that is a very important point. We must be careful not to put our kind volunteers in a position where they feel overwhelmed or unsafe.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"If we expand, we must consider that the building is not the center of the world. The distance for some is now far too great.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,Why did we stop the outreach? The sheets say forty people came! That's a whole classroom! We should just do that again but better!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Jonathan, if we move services outward, we must ensure the funding is operational, not just a one-time grant. Otherwise, we are merely building a house of cards.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"Exactly. If we implement a service that requires specialized certification or supervision, we cannot simply assume the staff will ""figure it out"" on the fly.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"I feel we should choose a path that does not depend on the buses or the roads being open. A service that comes to the people, perhaps?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,A mobile or remote service would alleviate the burden of the distance. It would be a gentle way to bridge the gap for the outer wards.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"Yes! Like the outreach! But we have to make sure we don't lose the files this time. We need a big, bright list so nothing gets forgotten!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I am inclined to agree, provided the funding is structured as a recurring operational cost. We cannot afford another ""successful"" project that dies in year two.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"I can support a mobile service, but only if we include a budget for professional training. We cannot expect the current staff to absorb the management of it.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,It sounds like we are all finding a common path. Let us be mindful of the people who feel forgotten in the winter.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I find peace in the idea of the library reaching out, rather than waiting for the world to find its way to us.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'm just glad we looked at the old papers! It's like a map to the future!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"A map, perhaps, but let us ensure the fuel for the journey is not a temporary loan.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"I will remain cautious, but I believe we can make this work if we prioritize the human capacity over the mere idea of the service.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
