59,3,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Option A seems the most caring. It brings the library to those who cannot travel, and it does not rely on the county's bus schedules.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,I strongly support Option A. It addresses the isolation of the outer wards and removes the physical barrier of our building's location.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,Option A is just like the outreach stops! We know it works because the old sheets said so! Let's do the one that people actually liked!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A is the most logical choice for reach, though I shall be watching the vehicle running lines very closely. It is the most sustainable if funded correctly.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Option A is feasible, but only if the driver and staff are properly trained. Option B would be a disaster given our lack of current tool certification.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"I am glad we all agree. It feels like a warm embrace for the whole community, not just those who live nearby.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,It is a quiet victory for accessibility. We are no longer deciding who can reach us; we are deciding how to reach them.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,I want to help pick the books for the van! Can we have a section for adventure stories? Please?,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, I believe your enthusiasm for the collection will be an asset, provided we don't forget to budget for the fuel and the tires.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"I will insist that the staffing for the mobile branch is a dedicated role, not an addition to the current branch managers' duties.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, that is a very thoughtful addition. We must take care of our staff as much as we take care of our patrons.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. A calm and sustainable pace is the only way to ensure the service lasts.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm just happy we aren't doing the photo thing again. That was a big mess! Option D sounds like that mess!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed, Option D is a digital rabbit hole that often consumes budgets without providing tangible community value. Option A is far more grounded.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,"I am satisfied. As long as the operational requirements are explicitly planned, Option A is the most responsible choice.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
